@startuml 03-abilities-combat
!pragma layout smetana
title Abilità e combattimento — Strategy data-driven

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class "configs/abilities/*.yaml" as AbilityYaml <<YAML>>

package "Configurazione e creazione" {
  class AbilityLoader <<Loader>> {
    + loadAbility(stream): AbilityConfiguration
  }
  class AbilityConfiguration <<DTO>>
  class AbilityFactory <<Strategy Registry>> {
    + {static} getStrategy(key): AbilityStrategy
  }
}

package "Abilità runtime" {
  interface SpecialAbility
  class DataDrivenAbility {
    - config: AbilityConfiguration
    - strategy: AbilityStrategy
    + perform(user, target, level): void
  }
  interface AbilityStrategy <<Strategy>> {
    + execute(context, config): void
  }
  class DamageStrategy
  class HealStrategy
  class AbilityContext
}

package "Combattimento" {
  class BattleController <<Controller>>
  class BattleModel <<Service>> {
    + executePlayerAttack(attacker, target): void
    + executePlayerSpecialAbility(attacker): void
    + executeUseItem(user, item, target): void
    + executeEnemyTurn(): void
  }
  enum BattlePhase <<Lifecycle State>>
  class Player <<external>>
  class Enemy <<external>>
  class Collectible <<external>>
  class BattleScreen <<Boundary>>
}

AbilityYaml --> AbilityLoader
AbilityLoader --> AbilityConfiguration
AbilityFactory o-- AbilityStrategy
DataDrivenAbility --> AbilityFactory : seleziona per chiave
DataDrivenAbility *-- AbilityConfiguration
DataDrivenAbility --> AbilityStrategy
SpecialAbility <|.. DataDrivenAbility
AbilityStrategy <|.. DamageStrategy
AbilityStrategy <|.. HealStrategy
AbilityStrategy --> AbilityContext

BattleController --> BattleModel
BattleScreen --> BattleController
BattleScreen --> BattleModel
BattleModel --> BattlePhase
BattleModel o-- "1..2" Player
BattleModel o-- "1..*" Enemy
BattleModel --> SpecialAbility
BattleModel --> Collectible

note bottom of AbilityStrategy
Pattern principale: Strategy.
La force è sostituire l'algoritmo di effetto senza cambiare
DataDrivenAbility o BattleModel.
BattlePhase rende esplicito il lifecycle, ma non è un GoF State
polimorfico: resta un enum controllato dal modello.
end note
@enduml
